.TH AURA\-HOOK 7 "2026-08-07" "Aura 0.1.0" "Aura Manual"
.SH NAME
aura\-hook \- external hook rules: stream alerts, events, and asks into Aura
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aura hook run \-\-rules <name.toml> \-\- <command>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Standalone processes can reach Aura over its local control socket by running a
command through a hook ruleset. Aura tails the command's stdout, writes every
line to a log, matches lines against your rules, and fires the resulting
actions (an \fBevent\fR into the cognitive pipeline, a direct \fBnotify\fR
message, or a \fBask\fR that posts Discord buttons and waits for a decision).
.PP
The wrapper exits with the child command's exit code. Hook commands need no
Discord access and no credentials; they speak over
~/.local/state/aura/aura.sock (mode 0600).
.SH RULES FILES
Rules live at ~/.config/aura/hooks/<name>.toml. A bare ruleset name passed to
\-\-rules resolves to that path; an explicit path (containing a slash) is used
as\-is.
.PP
A rules file has a header naming the source, then one or more
.B [[rule]]
tables. Every rule binds a regex \fBmatch\fR against each output line, a
\fBlane\fR, rendered \fBtext\fR, and a \fBtarget\fR.
.PP
.nf
name = "my-collector"          # log file: ~/.local/state/aura/hooks/my-collector.log
source = "collector"           # provenance tag; must be non-empty

[[rule]]
name = "blocked"               # provenance: [hook:collector/blocked]
match = "BLOCKED: (.+)"        # regex against each stdout/stderr line
lane = "ask"                   # event | notify | ask
target = "default"             # default | domain:<name>
text = "The collector is blocked: {1}. Resolve it in the browser."
buttons = ["Resolved", "Abort"]
ttl_minutes = 30               # optional, default 60

[[rule]]
name = "progress"
match = "PROGRESS (\\\\d+)"
lane = "event"                 # goes through the cognitive pipeline
target = "default"
text = "Collector progress: {1}"

[[rule]]
name = "finished"
match = "DONE"
lane = "notify"                # direct message, no model in the loop
target = "domain:projects"
text = "The collector finished."
.fi
.SS Required fields per rule
.TP
.B name
Unique within the file; used in provenance and the external id.
.TP
.B match
Regular expression compiled at load time. An invalid pattern is a load error,
not a runtime surprise.
.TP
.B lane
One of \fBevent\fR, \fBnotify\fR, \fBask\fR. A rule with any other value fails
to load.
.TP
.B target
.B default
or
.B domain:<name>
(must match a configured delivery target).
.TP
.B text
Template rendered from the match (see TEMPLATES).
.SS Optional fields
.TP
.B buttons
List of button labels for \fBlane = "ask"\fR. Defaults to ["Resolved", "Abort"].
.TP
.B ttl_minutes
How long an ask stays clickable. Default 60.
.TP
.B external_id
Template used as the dedupe key for event/notify (default
\fB<source>:<rule>:<rendered text>\fR) and as the correlation id for ask
(default \fB<source>-<rule>-<millis>\fR).
.SH TEMPLATES
Text and external_id templates substitute:
.PP
.nf
{line}  the whole output line
{0}     the whole regex match
{1}..   capture groups, left to right
.fi
.PP
Referencing a group that does not exist is a render error: the wrapper logs it
rather than silently dropping the action. To escape a literal brace, write a
non\-numeric token (for example "{not-a-group}") which is left verbatim.
.SH LANES
.TP
.B event
Subject goes through event_ingest and the cognitive pipeline (dedupe, model
attention decision, delivery). Use for progress and ambient signals where the
model judges urgency.
.TP
.B notify
Delivered directly to the target (deduped, ledgered), prefixed with
[hook:<source>/<rule>] provenance. No model in the loop. Use for time\-critical
alerts.
.TP
.B ask
Posts Discord buttons for the target and blocks until a button is clicked, the
TTL expires, or Aura is unreachable. On resolution the chosen label is written
to ~/.local/state/aura/hooks/decisions/<correlation_id> for the calling process
to poll. Transient socket failures are retried with backoff until the TTL.
.SH FILES
.TP
~/.config/aura/hooks/<name>.toml
Rules definitions.
.TP
~/.local/state/aura/hooks/<name>.log
Tee of every line the wrapped command printed.
.TP
~/.local/state/aura/hooks/decisions/<correlation_id>
Materialized choice when an ask resolves.
.SH INTROSPECTION
.B aura hooks
Lists registered rulesets (from the hooks config directory) and recent event
sources with counts. \fBaura asks\fR lists pending and recent asks.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP 1. 4
Watch a build and alert on failure:
.PP
.nf
aura hook run --rules build -- 'make && make test'
.fi
.PP
with a rule matching "^FAIL" on lane notify.
.IP 2. 4
Ad\-hoc rules file:
.PP
.nf
aura hook run --rules /tmp/my-rules.toml -- 'python collector.py'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
aura(1), aura\-config(5), docs/architecture/external-hooks.md,
docs/decisions/038-external-hook-layer.md
